1
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:03,160
<i>Yo.</i>

2
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:04,960
<i>I'm not Yo.</i>

3
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:07,440
<i>I saw the three of them.</i>

4
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:10,080
<i>They were tortured to death.</i>

5
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,120
<i>But what they resent even more is...</i>

6
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:14,880
<i>that their trapped souls can never be reborn.</i>

7
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,040
<i>Is there any way to fix this?</i>

8
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:17,280
<i>The three from the past,</i>

9
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:20,520
<i>Lert, Bulan, and Sroi must die.</i>

10
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:22,000
<i>Bitch Bulan killed you!</i>

11
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,760
<i>A fool like you is bound to be betrayed.</i>

12
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:25,920
<i>Kadkao!</i>

13
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:29,880
<i>- I'm not Kadkao!
- Kadkao... Kadkao...</i>

14
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:32,826
<i>I'm not Kadkao!</i>

15
00:01:32,826 --> 00:01:35,760
What happened to you isn't unusual.

16
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:38,093
The spirits are targeting you.

17
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:42,280
But they asked us to help Kadkao.

18
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,760
I just went to see Yo.

19
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:45,600
She talked about Kadkao too.

20
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:49,000
It's up to you two now.

21
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,746
You must keep your minds strong.

22
00:01:51,746 --> 00:01:53,520
But if you want my advice,

23
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:56,763
if it's not your business, stay out of it.

24
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:00,466
That's what you're telling me, right?

25
00:02:00,466 --> 00:02:02,160
Even if it is your business,

26
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:04,240
end it while you still can.

27
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,050
Yes.

28
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:09,360
The living and the dead should remain apart.

29
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:12,600
Especially vengeful spirits.

30
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:16,550
Their minds are consumed by revenge.

31
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:20,120
I'm worried about you.

32
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,496
I'll put an end to it.

33
00:02:22,496 --> 00:02:23,840
Make sure you do.

34
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,720
Buddhism teaches us to end suffering,

35
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:28,150
not cling to it.

36
00:02:37,146 --> 00:02:38,360
[Police]

37
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:40,440
After what happened to you the other day,

38
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:44,880
my friend who's a geospatial analyst
sent me these images.

39
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:46,960
Now I'm starting to wonder.

40
00:02:47,776 --> 00:02:49,390
Shit!

41
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:55,040
Why do these people look just like Nat's group?

42
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:56,800
And those three look...

43
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:59,280
just like the people I saw the other day.

44
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:01,440
<i>How can I help you?</i>

45
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,680
<i>Please help Kadkao.</i>

46
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:05,960
But these aren't real images.

47
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:11,440
My friend used old land records,
terrain data, and historical records,

48
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:15,560
then fed the raw data into AI to reconstruct

49
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:19,540
what this area looked like
over a hundred years ago.

50
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,840
But here's the strange part.

51
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:26,640
None of the raw data described any faces.

52
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:29,613
We didn't even give the AI
photos of Nat's group.

53
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:33,653
The AI generated these faces on its own.

54
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:40,053
Can you believe it?

55
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:45,120
When I stare at them long enough,

56
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:48,760
I feel like they're still alive.

57
00:04:50,275 --> 00:04:52,775
[Nat]

58
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,506
<i>Disgusting!</i>

59
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,640
How could you sink this low, Nat?

60
00:05:50,322 --> 00:05:52,600
Nat's really stressed out.

61
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:55,040
I'm just being honest.

62
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:59,320
I have no idea how it video-called you.

63
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:01,653
It must've been a ghost.

64
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,080
Ghost or human, I don't care.

65
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,440
Just tell Nat to come sign the divorce papers.

66
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:25,160
I'd rather die than divorce you.

67
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:27,053
But I'm divorcing you.

68
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:31,891
Nat! Nat! Get off me!

69
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:34,240
No! I love you, Yo.

70
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:36,760
But I don't love you!

71
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:39,153
Get off me... Get off me!

72
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,493
Yo!

73
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:50,680
Nat, let me go!

74
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:54,586
Let go... Nat!

75
00:06:57,240 --> 00:07:01,760
Yo! Yo, wait!

76
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:06,146
Yo.

77
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,546
Yo.

78
00:07:15,634 --> 00:07:18,070
<i>I'm tired of it.</i>

79
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:20,108
<i>Every day with Yo is a problem.</i>

80
00:07:21,414 --> 00:07:23,600
<i>It's better if she has someone else.</i>

81
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,400
<i>If Yo were sweet and easygoing,
I wouldn't do anything to her.</i>

82
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:30,440
<i>But if I can't control her,
I'll use that guy as leverage.</i>

83
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:31,840
Yo... I...

84
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,613
Will you divorce me, or do I have to sue you?

85
00:07:40,493 --> 00:07:42,000
Do whatever you want.

86
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,886
But I'm telling you,

87
00:07:43,886 --> 00:07:46,409
I will never divorce you.

88
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,600
Yes, Pete?

89
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:58,914
Yo, can you come to the station right now?

90
00:07:59,852 --> 00:08:01,080
What is it?

91
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:02,600
I have a new lead.

92
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:06,280
It's related to what you dreamed about.

93
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,520
I want you to see it for yourself.

94
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:10,127
I'll be right there.

95
00:08:18,475 --> 00:08:20,920
[Police Station for the People]

96
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,613
Pete.

97
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:26,321
Someone's waiting for you out front.

98
00:08:26,321 --> 00:08:28,106
Who?

99
00:08:34,089 --> 00:08:37,000
- This is a police station!
- Good.

100
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,785
Then everyone can hear this.
Stay away from my wife.

101
00:08:42,413 --> 00:08:44,880
Saying that is disrespectful to your wife.

102
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:46,971
I respect my wife.

103
00:08:46,971 --> 00:08:49,960
I don't respect a man who goes after her.

104
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,680
You just called Yo.

105
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:54,059
Don't deny it.

106
00:09:02,518 --> 00:09:05,209
Stay away from my wife.

107
00:09:05,209 --> 00:09:07,480
Or I'll beat the hell out of you.

108
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:09,003
Try me.

109
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:21,040
Yo.

110
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:23,026
I'm sorry.

111
00:09:23,026 --> 00:09:25,009
He and I just had a fight.

112
00:09:27,616 --> 00:09:29,173
Pete.

113
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,493
The lady's here.

114
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,960
Let's go.

115
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:40,440
This is Aunt Win.

116
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,678
She used to live
near the great-grandfather's house.

117
00:09:42,678 --> 00:09:45,807
Recently, her nephew had a strange dream.

118
00:09:47,306 --> 00:09:51,242
My nephew dreamed about three people.

119
00:09:51,242 --> 00:09:53,977
They seem to be our ancestors.

120
00:09:53,977 --> 00:09:58,000
They told him their souls were trapped.

121
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,098
Keng studied art.

122
00:10:01,098 --> 00:10:03,386
He drew this.

123
00:10:18,188 --> 00:10:20,650
They're exactly like the people I saw
in my dreams.

124
00:10:23,153 --> 00:10:24,853
Yohd.

125
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:30,315
Pan.

126
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,720
<i>We won't try to run away again.</i>

127
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,186
Sali.

128
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:46,920
Where is your nephew now?

129
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:49,640
In the hospital.

130
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:52,733
He's suffering from depression.

131
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:28,546
Go see it for yourself...

132
00:11:28,546 --> 00:11:30,386
Kadkao.

133
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:35,240
This girl's name is Kadkao, sir.

134
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:38,440
Her parents are addicted to gambling.

135
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:41,200
They owe our gambling house twenty chang.

136
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,520
They can't repay the principal.

137
00:11:44,288 --> 00:11:47,040
So they gave us their daughter
to work off the interest.

138
00:11:47,846 --> 00:11:49,600
Come here.

139
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:19,813
Your parents sold you?

140
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,704
She's quite pretty.

141
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:27,301
But there's defiance in her eyes.

142
00:12:28,569 --> 00:12:30,253
Sroi!

143
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:33,533
Send her to the kitchen.

144
00:12:33,533 --> 00:12:36,160
Make her chop wood and carry water.

145
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:38,653
Don't let her come up here.

146
00:13:03,933 --> 00:13:06,760
Is there something I can do for you?

147
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,680
What brings you down here, my lady?

148
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:13,240
I just came to see if our new debt slave

149
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:17,963
is worth the twenty chang Master paid for her.

150
00:13:23,884 --> 00:13:26,510
Palm sugar, cooked down nice and thick...

151
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:30,000
It smells so sweet.

152
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,546
Anyone would be tempted to have a taste.

153
00:14:11,798 --> 00:14:14,719
I know my place.

154
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:17,520
Good.

155
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,907
If you ever forget your place,

156
00:14:21,228 --> 00:14:23,520
I won't drip it on your hands.

157
00:14:24,907 --> 00:14:27,466
I'll pour it over your face.

158
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:10,906
So I was Kadkao.

159
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:26,906
What about the marital property?

160
00:15:29,327 --> 00:15:32,186
He just transferred the house to me.

161
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:38,976
Is this house marital property?

162
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,480
No.

163
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:46,666
It was given to you as a gift.

164
00:15:46,666 --> 00:15:48,560
What if I want to sell it?

165
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:50,440
I'm afraid you can't.

166
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,653
Why not?

167
00:15:52,653 --> 00:15:54,890
Because your husband...

168
00:15:54,890 --> 00:15:56,080
[Nat Thanahirankit - Life Usufruct]

169
00:15:56,080 --> 00:16:00,560
registered a life usufruct on the title deed.

170
00:16:03,815 --> 00:16:06,560
What's a life usufruct?

171
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:11,145
It gives him rights over the property
for the rest of his life.

172
00:16:11,145 --> 00:16:15,920
Even after you divorce,
he still has the right to live there

173
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:18,560
or rent the house out.

174
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:25,333
Having your name on the title deed
doesn't give you complete control.

175
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:28,760
So there's nothing I can do?

176
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,880
If you really want to sell it,

177
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:33,600
you'll have to wait until he dies.

178
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,904
Then you'll have full control of the property.

179
00:16:43,628 --> 00:16:46,186
I guess I've been a fool again.

180
00:16:49,107 --> 00:16:51,520
I think he transferred it to you

181
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:54,426
to show you he was sincere.

182
00:16:54,426 --> 00:17:01,560
But he registered a life usufruct
to protect his own rights.

183
00:17:04,157 --> 00:17:06,693
So you can't force him out.

184
00:17:08,744 --> 00:17:10,702
If I can't make him leave,

185
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:14,760
then I'm the one who has to go.

186
00:17:19,278 --> 00:17:21,638
[Nat Thanahirankit - Life Usufruct]

187
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,976
It's a court summons.

188
00:17:30,976 --> 00:17:33,266
Yo is suing you for divorce.

189
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:07,546
<i>Fish rice soup, Yo's favorite.</i>

190
00:18:07,546 --> 00:18:09,560
<i>Thank you, Chef.</i>

191
00:18:11,193 --> 00:18:13,305
<i>Try it.</i>

192
00:18:13,305 --> 00:18:15,200
<i>Thank you.</i>

193
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,480
Yo.

194
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:12,610
Sorry to bother you again.

195
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:16,816
Do you know of any place
that's not too expensive?

196
00:19:17,386 --> 00:19:19,680
You can stay at my place.

197
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:21,964
I'm hardly ever home.

198
00:19:21,964 --> 00:19:24,163
I usually sleep at the station.

199
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:31,720
I'd feel bad imposing on you.

200
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:33,706
Not at all.

201
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:39,840
Thank you so much.

202
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:49,386
Here's the house key.

203
00:19:49,386 --> 00:19:52,320
I'll call before I come over.

204
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:54,000
Thank you.

205
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:10,400
<i>Why did you do this to me, Nat?</i>

206
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:12,891
<i>I'm sorry, Yo.</i>

207
00:20:12,891 --> 00:20:16,480
<i>I promised. I'll be the husband you deserve.</i>

208
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,960
<i>Please, don't leave me.</i>

209
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:20,121
<i>Please, don't leave me. I'm begging you.</i>

210
00:20:20,121 --> 00:20:22,373
<i>Please...</i>

211
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:32,000
<i>How long do I have to play dumb</i>

212
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,160
<i>before you leave her?</i>

213
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:36,280
<i>I have to work with her.</i>

214
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:37,760
<i>What about me?</i>

215
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:39,440
<i>I'm doing all this for you!</i>

216
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:42,811
<i>The more you say that, the more it hurts.</i>

217
00:20:42,811 --> 00:20:45,400
<i>Yo, I'm really just working there.</i>

218
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:47,440
<i>I've been working myself to the bone lately.</i>

219
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:49,702
<i>You must know why.</i>

220
00:21:06,144 --> 00:21:10,720
Have a drink, Nat. You look really stressed.

221
00:21:22,556 --> 00:21:24,826
I don't understand myself.

222
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:28,440
Why do I feel...

223
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,346
so heartbroken right now?

224
00:21:46,339 --> 00:21:48,733
I'm going home to Yo.

225
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:53,480
And whatever was between the three of us...

226
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,560
ends here.

227
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:05,800
I understand.

228
00:22:08,040 --> 00:22:10,746
If you love Yo that much,

229
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:13,798
I'll step aside.

230
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:31,107
But before you go,

231
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:35,586
will you have this drink for me?

232
00:22:35,586 --> 00:22:38,800
To the love we once shared.

233
00:22:40,271 --> 00:22:42,106
I promise...

234
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:45,600
I won't try to hold you back anymore.

235
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:29,600
Thank you for understanding.

236
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:08,040
You think I'd let you go that easily, Nat?

237
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:11,386
You'll never escape from me.

238
00:24:57,480 --> 00:24:59,840
I'm still here?

239
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:02,403
You drank a lot last night.

240
00:25:06,564 --> 00:25:09,200
Warm ginger tea for your hangover.

241
00:25:28,065 --> 00:25:30,600
I think you should divorce Yo peacefully.

242
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:32,600
I told you. I'm not divorcing her.

243
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:38,708
I heard Yo is seeing Pete.

244
00:25:38,708 --> 00:25:40,986
Just let her go.

245
00:25:42,120 --> 00:25:43,798
No!

246
00:25:43,798 --> 00:25:46,240
Now that I know,
I definitely won't divorce her.

247
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:07,053
Giving Nat drugs won't hurt him, right?

248
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:10,720
This should be fine.

249
00:26:27,280 --> 00:26:29,186
Yo...

250
00:26:44,840 --> 00:26:47,173
I'm not letting you go anywhere, Kadkao.

251
00:26:50,097 --> 00:26:52,080
Please let me go, Master.

252
00:26:52,771 --> 00:26:55,066
I'm only a debt slave.

253
00:26:56,800 --> 00:27:01,040
I want you to have only my lady.

254
00:27:01,040 --> 00:27:03,280
Then this house will be peaceful.

255
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:08,840
Peaceful?

256
00:27:08,840 --> 00:27:11,400
But if I can't have you,

257
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:13,693
I'd be as good as dead.

258
00:27:16,262 --> 00:27:18,373
I love you, Kadkao.

259
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:25,093
I love you, Yo.

260
00:27:29,184 --> 00:27:31,291
I've given in to you.

261
00:27:31,291 --> 00:27:33,533
I've never given in to anyone.

262
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:37,360
You can't do this to me.

263
00:27:39,078 --> 00:27:40,813
Do you hear me?

264
00:27:41,387 --> 00:27:43,199
I won't accept this.

265
00:28:07,800 --> 00:28:11,280
Sorry Nat dragged this out for so long.

266
00:28:13,160 --> 00:28:16,389
But he's ready to divorce you now.

267
00:28:16,389 --> 00:28:18,573
Then tell him to meet me
at the district office.

268
00:28:20,587 --> 00:28:23,085
If you don't want to see Nat,

269
00:28:23,085 --> 00:28:25,746
you can sign a divorce agreement

270
00:28:25,746 --> 00:28:28,057
at any district office.

271
00:28:28,057 --> 00:28:30,613
You can register separately
so it won't be awkward.

272
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:36,416
Fine by me.

273
00:28:37,103 --> 00:28:39,723
Congratulations on your freedom.

274
00:28:48,280 --> 00:28:49,919
Wait.

275
00:28:52,280 --> 00:28:54,360
Tell Nat to meet me at the district office.

276
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:55,880
Let's get this over with quickly.

277
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:58,613
No need to complicate things with paperwork.

278
00:28:59,907 --> 00:29:01,400
Fine.

279
00:29:17,720 --> 00:29:23,680
[District Office - Bangkok Metropolitan]

280
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:27,033
Yotaka Thanahirankit.

281
00:29:27,033 --> 00:29:28,399
Yes.

282
00:29:29,948 --> 00:29:32,560
Nat Thanahirankit.

283
00:29:35,760 --> 00:29:39,066
Nat, the officer is asking you.

284
00:29:41,720 --> 00:29:43,133
Yes.

285
00:29:44,271 --> 00:29:46,600
You don't look well.

286
00:29:46,600 --> 00:29:53,826
To register a divorce, both parties
must be fully conscious and aware.

287
00:29:55,280 --> 00:29:57,280
He's sick.

288
00:29:57,280 --> 00:30:01,019
He's been heartbroken
and hasn't slept for days.

289
00:30:01,019 --> 00:30:03,466
He's devastated about the divorce.

290
00:30:06,363 --> 00:30:07,640
Nat.

291
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:11,083
Do you confirm that you're divorcing
of your own free will,

292
00:30:11,083 --> 00:30:13,910
and no one is forcing you?

293
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:21,055
<i>Yo doesn't love you.</i>

294
00:30:21,055 --> 00:30:23,560
<i>Divorce her.</i>

295
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:25,826
<i>Divorce her.</i>

296
00:30:31,280 --> 00:30:32,920
I...

297
00:30:33,840 --> 00:30:35,280
do.

298
00:30:37,640 --> 00:30:43,573
If you've settled the property matters,
please sign here.

299
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:48,720
Nat, sign it. Go on.

300
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:25,200
Yotaka, please sign here.

301
00:31:36,120 --> 00:31:38,533
Go ahead and sign, Yo.

302
00:32:01,733 --> 00:32:03,675
I've changed my mind.

303
00:32:03,675 --> 00:32:04,840
I'm not divorcing him.

304
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:06,395
What's wrong with you?

305
00:32:07,720 --> 00:32:12,120
Stop. If you can't agree,
please settle this outside.

306
00:32:12,120 --> 00:32:15,040
Let me know if you change your mind.

307
00:32:15,040 --> 00:32:16,502
What a waste of time!

308
00:32:34,417 --> 00:32:36,960
Nat looked terrible.

309
00:32:37,577 --> 00:32:39,089
He seemed barely conscious.

310
00:32:39,089 --> 00:32:42,426
I'm afraid Pam may have drugged him.

311
00:32:43,040 --> 00:32:45,120
If Nat really was drugged,

312
00:32:45,120 --> 00:32:47,704
this becomes an urgent criminal case,

313
00:32:47,704 --> 00:32:50,106
not just a family matter.

314
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:53,806
I'm afraid Pam might take Nat away.

315
00:32:55,080 --> 00:32:57,383
I'll keep watch from a distance.

316
00:32:57,383 --> 00:33:00,800
If they make a move or I find any evidence,

317
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:02,640
I'll call you right away.

318
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:04,625
Wouldn't it be better if I sent a detective?

319
00:33:04,625 --> 00:33:06,733
No.

320
00:33:06,733 --> 00:33:08,799
I don't want to make a big deal of it.

321
00:33:12,709 --> 00:33:14,493
[Nat]

322
00:33:22,133 --> 00:33:23,138
What is it, Nat?

323
00:33:23,138 --> 00:33:24,760
<i>I agreed to the divorce.</i>

324
00:33:24,760 --> 00:33:26,200
<i>Why wouldn't you go through with it?</i>

325
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:29,973
Because you looked sick.
You barely had any strength.

326
00:33:29,973 --> 00:33:33,760
<i>I'm fine. Tell me when you're ready to divorce.</i>

327
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:35,640
<i>The sooner, the better.</i>

328
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:38,560
<i>Then I can marry Pam.</i>

329
00:33:38,560 --> 00:33:40,333
<i>I love Pam.</i>

330
00:33:40,333 --> 00:33:42,000
<i>Do you understand, Yo?</i>

331
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:43,480
<i>If you don't want to see me</i>

332
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,920
<i>or Pam,</i>

333
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:47,938
I'll prepare the divorce papers.

334
00:33:47,938 --> 00:33:50,640
Sign them whenever you're ready.

335
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:52,813
<i>Then we can finally be done.</i>

336
00:34:05,040 --> 00:34:06,506
Are you okay?

337
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:24,480
I think I busted Pam.

338
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:26,466
Busted?

339
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:03,080
Nat,

340
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:05,120
have some water.

341
00:35:10,120 --> 00:35:11,759
No.

342
00:35:33,792 --> 00:35:37,880
[Nat]

343
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:40,040
[Yo]

344
00:36:06,235 --> 00:36:08,093
[Yo]

345
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:10,040
Answer it.

346
00:36:10,040 --> 00:36:12,090
[Yo]

347
00:36:12,090 --> 00:36:14,733
[This call will be recorded.]

348
00:36:16,307 --> 00:36:17,400
<i>Why are you calling?</i>

349
00:36:17,400 --> 00:36:19,240
<i>I'm busy. I have to go.</i>

350
00:36:19,240 --> 00:36:21,426
Wait, Nat.

351
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:26,920
I'm calling to tell you
I've changed my mind about the divorce.

352
00:36:27,786 --> 00:36:29,760
So when do you want to divorce?

353
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:33,960
You pick the date.

354
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:37,066
But when we go,

355
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:41,746
could you wear the first outfit
I ever bought you?

356
00:36:42,560 --> 00:36:44,905
<i>Do it for me one last time.</i>

357
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:50,040
That white shirt.

358
00:36:50,901 --> 00:36:52,751
You're so demanding.

359
00:36:52,751 --> 00:36:55,626
<i>Fine. I'll wear it.</i>

360
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:04,000
I never bought Nat a white shirt.

361
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:05,870
Got you.

362
00:37:23,786 --> 00:37:25,160
Hello, Yo.

363
00:37:25,160 --> 00:37:29,056
Pete, I have proof that
wasn't Nat I was talking to.

364
00:37:29,056 --> 00:37:31,600
It was an AI-cloned voice.

365
00:37:31,600 --> 00:37:33,000
Send me the audio file.

366
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:34,240
I'll have it checked.

367
00:37:34,240 --> 00:37:35,626
Okay.

368
00:37:37,675 --> 00:37:40,120
[Call with Nat]

369
00:37:40,120 --> 00:37:43,346
[Share with Pete]

370
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:02,826
Nat!

371
00:38:05,626 --> 00:38:07,160
Are you okay?

372
00:38:10,226 --> 00:38:11,600
Nat isn't well.

373
00:38:11,600 --> 00:38:13,080
I'm taking him to the hospital.

374
00:38:13,080 --> 00:38:14,226
Okay.

375
00:38:32,440 --> 00:38:35,960
<i>If you know anything else,
please give me a call.</i>

376
00:38:35,960 --> 00:38:37,560
<i>Sure, sir.</i>

377
00:38:38,720 --> 00:38:39,800
[Pol. Maj. Peerawich Sathitpong]
[Inspector (Investigation)]

378
00:38:59,829 --> 00:39:01,160
Hello?

379
00:39:01,160 --> 00:39:04,118
<i>Hello, Officer. I've seen Nat.</i>

380
00:39:04,118 --> 00:39:08,400
<i>He doesn't look well, just like you suspected.</i>

381
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:10,200
Where is he now?

382
00:39:10,200 --> 00:39:12,560
<i>Pam took him to the hospital.</i>

383
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:14,226
Thank you very much.

384
00:39:28,840 --> 00:39:32,230
Why did you bring Nat here?

385
00:39:40,080 --> 00:39:42,426
I'm taking him back to his own house.

386
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:46,680
The police and Yo
must be looking everywhere for Nat.

387
00:39:46,680 --> 00:39:48,866
I'd like to see what happens

388
00:39:48,866 --> 00:39:50,720
when they all show up

389
00:39:50,720 --> 00:39:54,053
and find Nat sleeping peacefully
in his own house.

390
00:39:55,482 --> 00:39:58,240
What can they possibly do to us?

391
00:40:01,200 --> 00:40:02,920
What's happening?

392
00:40:03,906 --> 00:40:05,360
I don't know.

393
00:40:05,360 --> 00:40:07,320
Let me try starting it again.

394
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:16,080
Oh! What's wrong with it?

395
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:47,213
We've been waiting so long for all of you.

396
00:40:59,520 --> 00:41:00,600
<i>How are you?</i>

397
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:02,240
<i>Fine, I guess.</i>

398
00:41:02,240 --> 00:41:04,920
<i>Seeing you cheat on me.</i>

399
00:41:04,920 --> 00:41:06,800
<i>You're talking just fine now.</i>

400
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:08,440
<i>Not drowsy or confused anymore?</i>

401
00:41:08,440 --> 00:41:11,000
<i>Can I have a strand of your hair for testing?</i>

402
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,160
<i>Police!</i>

403
00:41:12,160 --> 00:41:14,120
<i>If I keep the precepts
and dedicate merit to them,</i>

404
00:41:14,120 --> 00:41:16,306
<i>could it lessen the harm to Nat?</i>

405
00:41:16,306 --> 00:41:17,520
<i>I love you.</i>

406
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:19,613
<i>I only want to be with you.</i>

407
00:41:19,613 --> 00:41:24,440
<i>If Master Lert drinks too much of this,
it could kill him.</i>

408
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:26,380
<i>Kadkao! Kadkao!</i>
